-XoAAnfQ9.jpg", "height": 896}, {"width": 1204, "heightRatio": 82, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HW7Q2ZCWgAAsNVJ.jpg", "height": 996}], "linkEmbed": false, "replies": 0, "created": 1794515400000, "id": "2120977432778088624", "video": false, "poll": false, "user": {"profilePicture": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2099475340523626496/Pdt1aMU__normal.jpg", "displayName": "Scott Mechkowski", "username": "ScottMechkowski"}, "content": "\ud83d\udea8 ICE DOESN'T KIDNAP AND IT DOESN'T \"DISAPPEAR\" ANYONE. THE NARRATIVE IS THE POINT.\n\nThe New York Times and the open-borders lawyers say ICE is \"disappearing\" people. That's a lie.\n\nNobody disappeared. ICE knows exactly where every detainee is, and every one of them can pick up", "parentTweet": false, "likes": 217}, "images": false, "linkEmbed": {"image": "https://pbs.twimg.com/card_img/2120428749518704640/a69h7_JI?format=jpg&name=800x419", "domain": "www.washingtonexaminer.com", "description": "Police records debunk the viral claim that ICE abducted Martin Soto on a diaper run, proving he was arrested for domestic assault.", "title": "They called ICE \u2018kidnappers.\u2019 The paper proves otherwise", "url": "https://t.co/ljAHRW5cZA"}, "replies": 4, "created": 1794672454000, "id": "2121636163970548161", "video": false, "poll": false, "user": {"profilePicture": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2099475340523626496/Pdt1aMU__normal.jpg", "displayName": "Scott Mechkowski", "username": "ScottMechkowski"}, "content": "The \"disappeared\" narrative is still making the rounds, so let me say it again. ICE doesn't kidnap anyone. Every arrest leaves a paper trail: a charging document, a booking record, and a detainee locator anyone can search. I laid out the paperwork in the Washington Examiner:", "parentTweet": false, "likes": 158}}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1ATodl2cyP", "is_twitter": false,